# Written before the first `git add`, which is the gate that matters: a rule
# added after a file is tracked has no effect on it.

# The retired engine and the contaminated corpus were archived outside this
# repository on 2026-08-22 and are no longer present. These rules stay as a
# backstop in case anything is ever restored by accident.
_retired_contaminated/
scenario/
app/
core/
policy/
tools/
mallow_preview.html
run_local_demo.sh

# Credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*-key.json
*credentials*.json
service-account*.json
.gcloud/
.config/gcloud/
.firebase/

# Caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Full-resolution art masters stay on the Owner's machine. The nine approved,
# quantised runtime files live one directory above and keep the same names.
assets/art/Original/

# 🔴 The live journal — a person's own records.
#
# The rule here used to be `data/out/`, the generated-corpus directory of a
# retired design. It is not the directory the product writes to; that is
# `data/live/`, and it was never covered. Three documents have said since
# 2026-08-22 that all three ignore files excluded it. They did not. Fixed
# 2026-08-23 by excluding the whole tree, which cannot drift the same way again.
data/

# The demo seeder is COMMITTED, on purpose (戰略官 2026-08-23): a judge who
# cannot reproduce the autonomous leaf cannot verify the one thing this
# submission is about. `demo/seed.py` is a clean synthetic script and nothing
# else lives in there; what it *produces* goes to `data/`, which is ignored
# above. The Dockerfile's explicit COPY list keeps it out of the image without
# needing a rule here.

# The visual QA package — roughly 53MB of screenshots that settled the
# registration numbers (PRODUCT_DECISIONS 25: kept on the machine, out of the
# submission repository). The report itself is small and worth keeping.
qa/*
!qa/QA_REPORT.md
